{"id":"5e0db065132180df","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-probability.md","title":"Probability","display":"df-probability — Probability","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-probability","aliases":["58-df-probability","Probability"],"display":"df-probability — Probability","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-probability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-probability</span><span>Probability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-probability — Probability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F\\in V\">\\(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (probability-measure predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}probability} \\vdash \\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\mathbb P(\\Omega)=1\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}probability} \\vdash \\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\mathbb P(\\Omega)=1\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Probability: normalized measure (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}(\\Omega)=1\">\\(\\mathbb{P}(\\Omega)=1\\)</span>)</li>\n<li>Complement, finite-additivity, and monotonicity are downstream consequences of the probability measure axioms.</li>\n<li>Conditional: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}(A \\mid B) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B)/\\mathbb{P}(B)\">\\(\\mathbb{P}(A \\mid B) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B)/\\mathbb{P}(B)\\)</span></li>\n<li>Independence: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B) = \\mathbb{P}(A)\\mathbb{P}(B)\">\\(\\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B) = \\mathbb{P}(A)\\mathbb{P}(B)\\)</span></li>\n<li>Baye's: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}(B \\mid A) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\mid B)\\mathbb{P}(B)/\\mathbb{P}(A)\">\\(\\mathbb{P}(B \\mid A) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\mid B)\\mathbb{P}(B)/\\mathbb{P}(A)\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":